r can run `stall-recovery.md`. Does **not** run final-report, markers, or teardown.\n  - `--phase finalize`: runs Step 18b final-report refresh, optional marker body, closing token/timing marks, and teardown. **Never** re-runs the active-stall gate. Invoked only after prompt-side Step 18a.5 completes (or is skipped by its predicates).\n- **Orchestrator ordering** (prompt-side, not inside the wrapper):\n  1. After Step 17, print Step 18 breadcrumb.\n  2. `step-18.sh --phase gate --stall-tracking-memory \"${STALL_TRACKING:-false}\"`.\n  3. If `STALL_RECOVERY_REQUIRED=true`: **MANDATORY — READ ENTIRE FILE** `skills/implement/references/stall-recovery.md`; run the full 9-sub-step procedure. Do **not** run Step 18a.5 or `--phase finalize` on this path. After `CLEARED=true`, set in-memory `STALL_TRACKING=false`. After terminal recovery completes (`stall-recovery-terminal-report.env` exists), proceed without re-running `--phase gate`.\n  4. When the active stall gate is clear, recovery cleared, or terminal recovery finished: run the **Step 18a.5 — Escalation-success report gate** section unchanged (including `normalize-outcome` argv rules and skip predicates).\n  5. Bind prompt-side `STEP17_EMITTED_FOR_STEP18` before the finalize fence: `true` when `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/.step17-emitted` exists **or** Step 17 marker body was already emitted as top-level chat this run; otherwise `false`.\n  6. Finalize fence:\n     ```bash\n     bash \"$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/larch-run.sh\" skills/implement/scripts/step-18.sh --phase finalize --step17-emitted \"${STEP17_EMITTED_FOR_STEP18:-false}\"\n     ```\n  7. Parse finalize **captured Bash stdout** (sole contract surface after teardown removes the tmpdir):\n     - Primary Step 18 body path: extract the first balanced `---LARCH-SUMMARY-FINAL-BEGIN---` / `---LARCH-SUMMARY-FINAL-END---` pair; emit verbatim as plain chat markdown when non-empty.\n     - When `EMIT_BODY=true`, `WFR_RC=0`, and markers are absent/invalid despite a non-empty `summary-final.md` at finalize time: print `**⚠ Step 18: EMIT_BODY=true but marker pair missing from finalize stdout.**` Do **not** Read `summary-final.md` after teardown.\n     - Relay teardown tail records from captured stdout verbatim (same fields as live `SKILL.md` Step 18): `RENAME_BRANCH=...`, `RENAME_STATUS=...`, `ISSUE_URL=...`, `STASH_REF=...`, `SENTINEL_WRITTEN=...`, `FINALIZE_SUBCOMMAND=...`, `FINALIZE_WARNINGS=...`, and any sibling tail KVs the wrapper prints.\n     - Do not add free-form recap prose.\n- **Match the live SKILL path** for Step 18b: call `python3 \"$CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT/python/cli.py\" final-report step18b --implement-tmpdir \"$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR\"` only. Do **not** resurrect dormant `step-18b-final-report.sh` steps (`cleanup.sh --help`, `token report --full`, `timing telemetry-mark \"Step 18 — cleanup\"`).\n- **`set -e` tolerance in finalize**: wrap `final-report step18b --implement-tmpdir \"$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR\"` in `set +e` with explicit rc capture (mirror `step-16-17.sh` around `step-17.sh`). Relay `WFR_RC`, skip markers on failure, then **unconditionally** run closing marks + `restore-finalize-state` gate + teardown with the same `|| true` tolerance as `step-18-finalize.sh`. A step18b non-zero exit must not abort before token/timing marks or `implement-finalize teardown`.\n- **Gate predicate pin**: branch on the live inverted all-false-or-empty rule from `skills/implement/SKILL.md` (lines 860–861) and `skills/implement/references/stall-recovery.md` (line 39). A layer is **active** when its value is **not** `false` **and** **not** empty. Emit `STALL_RECOVERY_REQUIRED=true` when **any** layer is active; `false` only when all four are false or empty. Do **not** use a narrower `truthy()` table from `stall-recovery-report.sh`.\n- **Stream contract**: do **not** call `larch_quiet_init` in `step-18.sh`. Stall KVs, `STALL_RECOVERY_REQUIRED`, `EMIT_BODY` / `WFR_RC`, marker lines, teardown tail records, and teardown tail records must land on captured Bash stdou